ingredients:
  - "3/4 cup Bottle Gourd, grated"
  - "1 medium Onion, chopped"
  - "1 medium Tomato, chopped"
  - "5 tsp Bengal Gram Flour"
  - "1 dsp Rice Flour"
  - "2 dsp Oil"
  - "1 tbsp Ginger Paste"
  - "1 tsp Garlic Paste"
  - "2 tsp Coriander Powder"
  - "1 tsp Cumin Seed Powder"
  - "1 Green Chili, chopped"
  - "1/2 tsp Red Chili Powder"
  - "1/4 tsp Turmeric Powder"
  - "1/4 tsp Fenugreek Seeds"
  - "1/4 tsp Black Pepper Powder"
  - "1/4 tsp Garam Masala"
  - "Salt to taste"
instructions:
  - "Grate bottle gourd and chop green chillies, tomatoes, onions, and coriander leaves."
  - "Mix grated bottle gourd with gram flour, rice flour, salt, and turmeric powder. Form into small balls."
  - "Deep fry the kofta balls in hot oil until golden brown. Drain and set aside."
  - "Heat 1 dsp oil in a pan and sauté onions until golden brown."
  - "Add ginger-garlic paste and spices, stir well and cook for a few minutes."
  - "Add chopped tomatoes and cook until the moisture evaporates."
  - "Pour in 1 cup of water and simmer until the gravy thickens."
  - "Add the fried koftas to the gravy, mix well, and turn off the heat."
  - "Garnish with chopped coriander leaves and serve hot."
